ying if you  forgot to bring it to room temperature  you can actually heat a glass bowl in a  microwave and then turn that over on the  butter and that'll kind of slowly bring  the temperature of the butter up you  still want to have a good amount of  structure it'll be nice and smooth i  mean everyone knows what it's like to  get some nice room temperature butter on  a knife put that on some toast like my  god it's amazing if your butter is too  cold it's just never really going to  blend all that well i write sugar the  easiest way to describe to someone the  differences between white and brown  sugar are probably with chocolate chip  cookies if you're using a lot of white  sugar the cookies will actually spread a  lot more and become really crunchy  whereas if you want kind of a chewier  thicker cookie brown sugar is the way to  go it's got molasses in it has a nice  flavor so that's an easy way to kind of  tell the difference between white sugar  and brown sugar  a lot of american recipes will have you  measuring cups the way that you're  supposed to measure in cups is to spoon  the ingredient into the cup itself so  it's kind of a nice light mixture then  use the end of the spoon to level off  the cup because cups are measured on  volume if you pack the flour in really  tightly then you'll get more flour than  the recipe was intended for which is why  i actually prefer to use recipes that  are weighted and just use a cheap  kitchen scale to measure my ingredients  either way both should get you a good  result one cup of flour is about 125  grams the nice thing here too is that  you can kind of scoop a little bit out  make sure it's totally even and you're  getting a really accurate result every  time  the next thing you want to do before you  start baking is to prep your tin  i'm going to use a little knob of butter  to rub all down the bottom as well as  the sides of the pan this is going to  help brown the cake really nicely it's  also going to help get the c